# 8. Initial Documented Results

The first phase of the AIO CODE case study produced several observable results.

## Entity Recognition

AI systems that initially failed to clearly identify the intended Marii Cuadros entity later produced responses associated with the intended creator.

## Entity Disambiguation

The research documented cases in which the name was initially confused with other individuals before the intended entity became more distinguishable during subsequent retrieval tests.

## Cross-System Recognition

The intended entity was independently retrieved during context-reduced testing in multiple AI systems.

Observed systems included:

* ChatGPT
* Gemini
* Perplexity

## Search Visibility

Changes in search visibility were also observed during the documentation period.

## Distributed Information

Multiple public information nodes became associated with the same identity.

These results form the initial empirical basis of AIO CODE.

